                                "sense_id": "c56c3d72-bbd4-3c49-b946-178760de9d96",
                                "text": "[…] having upon sea borde greate sandes, which do make the harborough good, and bytwene the londing place and the towne is, at the leste, 40 score tayloures yardes, …"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4adda977-9d4f-4915-a6de-8df00a9ac01f",
                                "sense_id": "c56c3d72-bbd4-3c49-b946-178760de9d96",
                                "text": "[T]here aboutes dwelt greate multitudes of people half wilde, hiding thẽſelues in caues of the grounde, of ſmall ſtature, and very fearefull, for as ſoone as they ſawe them they fled into their holes, and that there was a great riuer and very good harborough."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ea92711-ef91-4161-848d-576a19fd86d3",
                                "sense_id": "c56c3d72-bbd4-3c49-b946-178760de9d96",
                                "text": "For all the sea coastes are ful of clear and glistering stones, & alabaster, and therefore it is full of good havens and harboroughs for ships."
                            }
                        ]
